{
  "case_id": "2010-10-114",
  "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Did we take the case on the assumption -- your -- your predecessor and you may disagree -- but did we take the case on the assumption that this was a frivolous cause of action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENKRANZ: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Mr. Fox has rock-solid legal claims against a police chief based upon facts that were strong enough to send that police chief to prison."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, wait. I mean, my goodness. You could say the same underlying facts justify, you know, a suit for -- for libel, and also justify a much -- a much greater suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if Mr. Fox had filed two -- two actions, the Federal claim in Federal court, the State claims in State court? Now, the Federal claim is handled in the same way that it was here. It's found to be frivolous."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: So how do you calculate that? I mean that -- that's what the question was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And I don't want to have you adopt this phrase, but just to clarify, are you saying that it's a but-for test, that you get only those fees for time that was -- that would not have been incurred but for the frivolous claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: In other words, you're saying that the lawyer has to keep account of -- now, if I'm going to spend time on \"under color of State law,\" I have to label that and figure the hours for that separately; similarly for whether Vice was an official policymaker, those hours that you are requiring that -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if the potential liability on the frivolous claim is much greater than the potential liability on the factually interrelated non- frivolous claims, and the defense argues that we spent a lot of time on -- a lot more time on these interrelated factual issues because of our fear of the greater liability on them than the frivolous claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I can imagine a district court being allowed to carve out an exception where they can say, well, we hired much more high-powered lawyers than we would have otherwise, and that was the -- responsible for an incremental increase."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court said it didn't have to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Much of Petitioner's eligibility argument rests on the notion that frivolous section 1983 claims imposed only modest or as he described them today, trivial burdens on defendants. And that's simply not the case. As amici who deal with these cases on a daily basis have confirmed, inclusion of even a frivolous section 1983 claim imposes significant additional burdens as part of the litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why do we start with your total fee and deduct down, rather than start where all the circuits are starting, which is to say, what can be attributed to that frivolous claim, which is the only thing you're entitled to fees from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Stancil, the first magistrate to get this case said explicitly that the discovery materials, the discovery in the Federal Court, would be usable in State court proceedings where those materials might aid in obtaining a judgment. So doesn't that have to be taken into account, that the discovery materials developed in Federal Court will now be used in the State court proceeding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think there's a more fundamental point, Your Honor, which is the District Court, in awarding fees, found there was no whiff of State law claims until the very -- very much the 11th hour in this claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, every other circuit except for the Sixth has dealt with the but-for test or some variant of it. Even the Fifth did it in this case and ruled in your favor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What matters is not how big -- how much of the cake was devoted to one claim versus another. What matters is how much more energy it takes to bake this particular sliver of the cake. It is all the same energy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I was wondering kind of as a starting point, and I don't know why you would fight so vigorously against the verbal formulation \"fairly attributable.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ROSENKRANZ",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, I -- I actually believe -- if I may answer the question, it is quite a bit easier to apply a but-for test and review it on appeal than it is to apply a test that is just a mishmash of factors over, if which the stakes are high enough, and they will be under Mr. Stancil's rule, there is an enormous incentive to litigate to death."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e089345c9b13d5383f46640d65d607e17acbfe5ee8cba93c991ed20a7958e911",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e089345c9b13-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-10-114",
      "confidence": 0.0,
